and specific sequence content. Interestingly, CRISPR loci evolved both via polarized addition of novel spacers after exposure to foreign genetic elements and via internal deletion of spacers. We hypothesize that the level of diversity is correlated with relative CRISPR activity and propose that the activity is highest for CRISPR1, followed by CRISPR3, while CRISPR2 may be degenerate. Globally, the dynamic nature of CRISPR loci might prove valuable for typing and comparative analyses of strains and microbial populations. Also, CRISPRs provide critical insights into the relationships between prokaryotes and their environments, notably the coevolution of host and viral genomes.\n                  <\/jats:p>","container-title":["Journal of Bacteriology"],"is-referenced-by-count":748},{"DOI":"10.1038\/nrmicro1793","title":["CRISPR \u2014 a widespread system that provides acquired resistance against phages in bacteria and archaea"],"issued":{"date-parts":[[2008,3]]},"author":[{"given":"Rotem","family":"Sorek","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Victor","family":"Kunin","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Philip","family":"Hugenholtz","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"container-title":["Nature Reviews Microbiology"],"is-referenced-by-count":800},{"DOI":"10.1016\/j.ijfoodmicro.2008.05.030","title":["Comparative analysis of CRISPR loci in lactic acid bacteria genomes"],"issued":{"date-parts":[[2009,4]]},"author":[{"given":"Philippe","family":"Horvath","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Anne-Claire","family":"Co\u00fbt\u00e9-Monvoisin","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Dennis A.","family":"Romero","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":